## Metadata
Author: G. H. F.
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-03-22
Number: 14
Notes: A 13-wide diamond with a cross-shaped centre panel (r5c6-8; r6-r8 c5-9; r9c6-8, shown as _) printed "No 14"; the intro also calls it "the fourteenth in FUN'S series". Number from the centre panel. Credit as printed: "It was sent in by "G. H. F.," of Putnam avenue, Brooklyn." Intro as printed: "Today's cross word puzzle, the fourteenth in FUN'S series, will be found different from any previous one. It was sent in by "G. H. F.," of Putnam avenue, Brooklyn. Fill in the small squares with words corresponding to the clews and definitions given below. The solution will be given in next week's FUN." The clue printed "2-28" is written 2-38, the squares its answer EVA runs between. Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_03_22_84.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_03_29_87.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.


